# Sports Live Player

A modern live sports dashboard with HLS support and a JSON-driven match list.

Features:
- Search and filter matches by status
- Live and upcoming match cards
- Multi-source HLS/MP4 playback
- Custom stream loader for manual URLs
- Dark sports TV style UI
- Works with local `data/matches.json` or remote JSON feeds

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Then open:

```text
http://localhost:4173
```

## Notes

- The app auto-loads `data/matches.json`.
- If the JSON file is missing or invalid, it falls back to demo streams.
- HLS is handled through `hls.js`.
- You can paste your own `.m3u8` or direct media URL in the custom source box.

## Supported match JSON structure

```json
{
  "matches": [
    {
      "title": "Team A vs Team B",
      "teams": "Team A vs Team B",
      "league": "League Name",
      "sport": "football",
      "status": "live",
      "viewers": "430",
      "server_urls": [
        "https://example.com/stream.m3u8",
        "https://example.com/backup.m3u8"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

This is a ready-to-use frontend for JSON and HLS live streaming.

## Optional deployment

You can deploy this as a static site on GitHub Pages, Netlify, Vercel, or any static host.

---

Built for the requested advanced sports streaming dashboard with JSON/HLS support and a dark premium TV-style experience.

